catalog_unicode_2026_09_20:
  status: implemented_and_fixture_tested_not_published
  evidence: ../TinyRustLM.com/artifacts/ecosystem-cleanup-20260912/catalog-unicode-review.json
  behavior: Canonical keys and values require Unicode scalar text. Reject lone surrogates in direct catalog validation; valid supplementary characters and combining sequences retain exact bytes across both projects. TinyRustLM also preserves BOMs for rejection.
  verification: All 88 MiniModel and 412 TinyRustLM Node checks pass; four TinyRustLM Edge checks and fourteen MiniModel observations pass with explicit Unicode cases at both viewports.
  visual: One historical screenshot comparison differed by fifteen select-border pixels. Controlled prior/current source captures match at each of three phases; preserve both outcomes. No style change or mask; no full-page visual claim.
  limits: Existing source-scan and publication gates remain open; current manifest regeneration and live readback are required. No model qualification, seed, NuGet or site publication; blocked cleanup remains untouched.

catalog_lifetime_2026_09_20:
  status: implemented_catalog_tested_publication_gate_blocked
  source_commit: 81f0b4c2bdee23abde6abd36d751e533b2425554
  evidence: artifacts/reports/catalog-lifetime-review-20260920.json
  behavior: One ten-second deadline covers both metadata streams and crypto observation; enforce one MiB and 4096 chunks before accumulation. Failure/cancellation stops sibling and stale work; late responses are disposed.
  verification: All 86 focused checks pass, including fourteen Edge observations. Eight existing desktop/mobile observations and screenshot identities exactly match the pre-edit baseline. Catalog line coverage is 91.95 percent.
  broader_gate: Committed-source run passes 117 of 121 checks; four publication checks stop at the known source_authority_scan_incomplete installer-link blocker. Nested Pester is 26 of 27. No test or gate was weakened.
  identity: Updated MiniModel pins for the reviewed September 19 canonical workspace-policy identity change; gate implementation is unchanged.
  boundary: Empty historical fixtures only; no real model, live seed, publication or full-page visual proof. WebCrypto and uncooperative tasks may finish after observation ends. Exact manifest regeneration and all publication gates remain required; preserve blocked cleanup.

static_seed_browser_execution_2026_09_19:
  status: local_apache_and_edge_cors_passed_not_published
  evidence: artifacts/reports/static-seed-browser-review-20260919.json
  verification: All 79 affected checks pass, including real Edge Fetch of six Apache bodies with exact exposed identity headers and SHA-256. Hidden-header, invalid-query and foreign-origin controls pass.
  lesson: HTTP header visibility differs from JavaScript visibility. ACAO is consumed internally and need not be exposed; the first test assumption was corrected without changing product validation or generated configuration.
  bounds: Only synthetic document navigations are intercepted; seed responses come from the separate real loopback Apache listener. Local-network permission is scoped to the two fixture origins, CORS remains enabled, and all owned browser/server output was removed after shutdown.
  limits: No public TLS, LiteSpeed, real composition installation, qualification, live seed or publication result. Existing source-scan and deletion blocks remain unchanged.

static_seed_apache_execution_2026_09_19:
  status: local_http_fixture_execution_passed_not_published
  evidence: artifacts/reports/static-seed-apache-review-20260919.json
  change: Real Apache execution found TRACE bypassing directory rules. Preparation now declares unverified server/vhost TraceEnable Off separately from htaccess; publicationAllowed remains false.
  verification: All 78 affected checks pass with zero skips, including six complete GET/HEAD transfers, exact nonduplicate identity headers, compression suppression and invalid-route/method controls on installed Apache 2.4.58 in OSM-Ubuntu. Generator coverage is 91.03 percent lines and 97.22 percent branches; shared companion-fixture reader is fully covered.
  environment: Separate owned loopback Apache instance; existing site configuration untouched. No software installation, Docker start, image download or remote mutation. Own PID/config exit was verified before bounded artifact cleanup.
  limits: Synthetic non-model bytes and local HTTP only. Alias proves URL spelling but not remote colon directory support. Real-browser CORS, TLS, LiteSpeed, qualification, publication authority and live seed remain open; prior source scan/deletion blocks remain unchanged.
  storage: Final Apache output removed 20 entries with 47439 logical file bytes; coverage output removed 6 entries with 1442889 logical bytes. No model/historical deletion or measured physical storage recovery.

static_seed_preparation_2026_09_19:
  status: historical_C33_generator_checkpoint_superseded_by_C34_local_apache_check
  source: tools/build-static-seed-plan.js
  contract: Current canonical Rust/companion six-member seed descriptor; piece-set identity is its exact SHA-256 with the final LF.
  behavior: Bounded stdin-only generator returns immutable member URLs, expected response identities and one hash-bound remote htaccess configuration. No local payload copy, credentials, network, signing, catalog renewal or upload; publicationAllowed stays false.
  verification: Cross-project canonical descriptor/profile tests and catalog regression checks; details and coverage are in artifacts/reports/static-seed-preparation-review-20260919.json.
  host_gate: deploy/static-seed.md requires actual override/module/path acceptance, six exact byte readbacks, real-browser CORS and qualified-model installation before advertising availability.
  limits: No Apache executable found on PATH; Docker Linux engine unavailable. No service started or image downloaded. C32 metadata readback is not static model-route evidence. Source scan still stops on the two previously policy-blocked TinyRustLM installer links; transport remains unbound and catalog authority expired.
  storage: Test/coverage output stays in owned MiniModel artifacts and is removed; no model payload or historical deletion and no measured storage recovery.

ecosystem_cleanup_2026_09_12:
  - Reconciled current guidance with the owner's authorization for initial MiniModel.org server seeds, stored only in D:\LLMs\TinyRustLM.
  - Preserved pending strict catalog/peer validation, canonical bytes, expiry, Ed25519 signatures, qualification and browser-admission descriptors, lifecycle revocation, and exact MiniModel.org seed-origin admission.
  - All 35 current catalog and cross-project contract tests passed. Test-only signatures and entries are synthetic; they do not establish model qualification or live peer transfer.
  - Current source is a prepared 1.1.2 candidate. The checked-in empty revision-3 catalog expired on 2026-09-09; no freshness, qualified starter, live seed or new deployment is claimed.
  - Production Companion ownership is TinyRustLM.com/dotnet/src/TinyRustLM.Companion, its CompanionHost tool, conversion/P2P projects and current Rust crates. Source acquisition, operation ownership, terminal reconciliation and browser wiring are implemented; real-model qualification and live seed proof remain open. MiniModel.org does not regain its retired pre-SLM2 native workspace.
  - Publication input now stays in bounded memory instead of copied site snapshots. The deployment Node launcher and generator have also been cleaned and exercised; release identities now bind the current public source and planned UTC publication date. Catalog freshness and real model/hosting work remain open. No transport was invoked.

publication_input_cleanup_2026_09_12:
  status: implemented_and_locally_verified_not_published
  source: tools/MiniModel.DeploymentCustody.psm1 and tools/deploy-site.ps1
  evidence: artifacts/reports/publication-input-review-20260912.json
  lessons: ../TinyRustLM.com/wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/ecosystem-experiment-lessons-2026-09-12.md C23
  change: Removed disk snapshot creation, Win32 snapshot directory identity, snapshot cleanup, BlobReader test hook and copied-source fixture case. Read bounded canonical Git/current bytes, bind exact materialized payloads in memory, and authenticate before upload or partial rollback.
  verification: All 53 Node checks and 24 nested Pester checks pass, zero skipped/cancelled. Actual Git/current catalog admission and stale-manifest rejection pass. Pester whole-module command coverage 238/545; publisher function execution uses actual parsed canonical definitions with transport mocked only in memory. No branch coverage or actual FTPS claim.
  temporary_output: Owned marker and Pester directories under artifacts/tests were physically removed; no copied source, local site stage or production receipt was created.
  unresolved_at_checkpoint: The manifest still bound 7e0a6eb6bf292ff69e3030adf1d229c811606ce9 and fails current catalog input admission. Transport is intentionally unbound. The subsequent publication-command checkpoint addresses the Node launcher and metadata generator. The catalog remains empty and expired, and release identity plus real model/hosting decisions remain open.
  storage: No historical files or model payloads were deleted in this checkpoint; no measured storage recovery.

publication_command_cleanup_2026_09_12:
  status: implemented_and_locally_verified_not_published
  evidence: artifacts/reports/publication-command-review-20260912.json
  lessons: ../TinyRustLM.com/wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/ecosystem-experiment-lessons-2026-09-12.md C24
  change: Manifest output is stdout-only with an exact 22-file public closure, current canonical/Git equality, authenticated Git blob bytes, bounded reads and deadlines. Ignored/untracked public extras are rejected. The publisher uses read-leased reviewed Node/gate/generator identities and excludes NODE_* startup settings from every child without changing the caller environment.
  canonical_bytes: Twenty public files had only CRLF differences; all 22 now exactly match existing committed bytes under explicit LF attributes. Public Git content and the 1.1.2 prepared release identity were not changed.
  verification: Complete affected suite has 64 Node and 27 nested Pester checks. Actual CLI metadata output, full 22-file JS/PowerShell materialization, hostile startup settings, owned-child timeout termination, current/old source rejection and no-output-path behavior are exercised. Exact final counts and limits are recorded in the compact review.
  publication_state_at_checkpoint: The actual read-only publisher reached stale-manifest rejection before public admission, credentials or receipt creation. Canonical manifest and unbound transport authority remain unchanged. No publication, real seed, model execution or measured storage recovery is claimed.

publication_binding_cleanup_2026_09_12:
  status: implemented_and_locally_verified_not_published
  public_source_commits: c73e2661eb1a6ba8a428c74c9016195992a1038d, df51ec03a52f4862471dd79a9d989405db5f251f
  evidence: artifacts/reports/publication-binding-review-20260912.json
  lessons: ../TinyRustLM.com/wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/ecosystem-experiment-lessons-2026-09-12.md C25
  change: Predecessor discovery remains bound to the immutable public receipt; candidate discovery has its own current identities. The 22-file manifest binds df51ec03a52f4862471dd79a9d989405db5f251f and planned UTC publication date 2026-09-13. Both JSON materializers use that date, preserve historical ledger entries, and leave source records prepared. Actual publication requires the reviewed date to equal the UTC transaction-start day.
  guidance: Public status/date claims now point to release JSON. Talisman, LLM guides and roadmap recognize authorized initial seeds and the existing canonical TinyRustLM companion. They do not claim deployed seeding or qualified models.
  verification: Complete affected suite passed 67 Node checks and 27 nested Pester checks, with no skips or cancellations. Full 22-file JS/PowerShell materialization, real Git predecessor identities, candidate substitution refusals, calendar/date disagreement and actual publisher child-process boundaries were exercised. Whole custody-module command coverage was 241/562; no new branch or generator/bootstrap coverage percentage is claimed.
  failed_checks: The first run passed 65/67 Node and 26/27 nested Pester checks; one assertion expected expired instead of the contract's stale wording, and one test incorrectly used the refreshed canonical manifest as its historical fixture. The latter now reads exact historical Git bytes without writing a copy.
  current_blockers: Verification rejects the empty revision-3 catalog's expired validity window through the actual browser contract before public admission or credentials. No validity window was renewed. Transport remains unbound. Real qualification and authorized seed hosting remain unresolved. A later publishing day needs reviewed metadata regeneration, not automatic renewal or replay.
  storage: Operation-owned test output was removed. No historical deletion, model acquisition, publication receipt or measured storage recovery was produced.

browser_catalog_cleanup_2026_09_12:
  status: implemented_and_locally_verified_not_published
  source_commit: d30114cac9326be104d0c441151caf0224425e3d
  evidence: artifacts/reports/browser-catalog-review-20260912.json
  lessons: ../TinyRustLM.com/wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/ecosystem-experiment-lessons-2026-09-12.md C26
  product: Loading or failed catalog authority clears previous actions, counts and filter callbacks. Failure shows a plain unavailable message and disables unusable controls. Verified retry restores the controls; superseded requests cannot overwrite newer ready or error state. CSS is unchanged.
  browser_tool: Removed system-temp profiles/screenshots, manual debugging-port management, broad command-line process matching and swallowed cleanup failures. Actual Edge uses existing canonical Playwright, a six-input ephemeral loopback server and one bounded owned artifact directory. Screenshots stay in memory; browsers and listeners close before ownership-checked removal. No arbitrary target/output arguments remain.
  verification: Full affected suite passed 74 Node and 27 nested Pester checks, zero skips/cancellations. Eight real Edge observations cover desktop/mobile current expiry and explicitly historical empty, failed reload and recovered empty states. Node coverage is 90.76 percent lines and 80.82 percent branches for catalog.js; 92.88 percent lines and 88.89 percent branches for the browser helper. This does not instrument JavaScript executed inside Edge.
  lessons_retained: Refresh the content-bound script URL with public script changes; isolate fixture clocks in fresh browsers; verify the operation's own output rather than a concurrently used artifacts parent; direct the coverage collector's parent process temp environment into owned canonical artifacts.
  limits: Historical fixture time is not catalog renewal, qualification or seed availability. Actual publication still rejects expired catalog authority before public admission and credentials. Transport is unbound; real model qualification and hosting remain open. No screenshots or browser profiles remain, no historical/model deletion occurred, and no measured storage recovery is claimed.

